WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.772 --> 00:00:02.578
- I am soaking wet.

00:00:02.578 --> 00:00:03.714
Hi, I'm Garrett.

00:00:03.714 --> 00:00:04.547
- And I'm Niki.

00:00:04.547 --> 00:00:06.446
- We're fascinated by
how other people live.

00:00:06.446 --> 00:00:07.851
- So we're gonna try to
find some really interesting

00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:09.092
living situations.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:10.712
- [Garrett] And live there,
see what it's like to have a

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:11.816
totally different lifestyle.

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:13.006
- [Niki] And see which ones
bring us closer together.

00:00:13.006 --> 00:00:14.434
- [Garrett] And push us further apart.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.453
- This week we live in a houseboat.

00:00:17.453 --> 00:00:18.631
- [Garrett] I thought we
were gonna be drifting

00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:19.503
a little bit closer.

00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:20.649
- [Niki] Yeah, you didn't paddle.

00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:22.095
- [Garrett] I wasn't paddling very hard.

00:00:22.095 --> 00:00:24.678
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.598 --> 00:00:31.431
- Hello.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.695
- Hello.

00:00:32.695 --> 00:00:33.528
- I'm Garrett.

00:00:33.528 --> 00:00:34.959
- And I'm Niki, nice to meet you.

00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:36.214
- Come on.

00:00:36.214 --> 00:00:39.144
My name is Lisa and I have
lived on the Coop De Villa

00:00:39.144 --> 00:00:40.819
for almost nine years.

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:43.153
It's the best move I've
ever made in my life.

00:00:43.153 --> 00:00:44.126
- Thank you.

00:00:44.126 --> 00:00:45.488
- There's one of the cats.

00:00:45.488 --> 00:00:46.339
- [Niki] Cat.

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:48.105
- That's Wally, she's the friendly one.

00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:53.006
- This houseboat has two cats
and I'm allergic to cats.

00:00:53.006 --> 00:00:54.789
- Cats on a boat, that's pretty funny.

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:55.977
- I've never been on a houseboat.

00:00:55.977 --> 00:00:57.810
I think I've seen houseboats before.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.393
- It's a house on water or
it's a boat you can live on?

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:04.030
- I guess I was on a cruise
ship, is that a houseboat?

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.893
- All these people that
live on boats here,

00:01:05.893 --> 00:01:07.391
this is considered the lobby.

00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:10.087
Everybody stops by here, so
if you're sitting out here

00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:11.740
enjoying yourselves.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.771
- [Garrett] Somebody else may stop by?

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:13.929
- [Lisa] Yeah, they all stop by.

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:16.320
- So my checklist for
living in the houseboat is

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.778
can I survive with cats?

00:01:17.778 --> 00:01:20.604
Is there a kitchen that's
big enough that I feel like

00:01:20.604 --> 00:01:22.219
I could live here?

00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:23.756
Is there a Garrett-sized shower?

00:01:23.756 --> 00:01:25.335
- This is the living room.

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.309
You can see there's lots of room in here.

00:01:27.309 --> 00:01:28.820
- [Nike] Yeah, this is awesome.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.169
- [Lisa] A full-sized kitchen.

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:31.869
- My checklist for living
in this houseboat is

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:33.895
that one, Garrett and I
have enough space to share.

00:01:33.895 --> 00:01:36.510
Two, that I have some
of those private spaces

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.819
where I can either close a
door or be in a different room.

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:41.686
Three, I live living in quiet places.

00:01:41.686 --> 00:01:43.721
I don't like living near
busy roads or highways

00:01:43.721 --> 00:01:45.544
and I don't know what it's
gonna be like on a marina.

00:01:45.544 --> 00:01:47.702
- A houseboat isn't really
like living on a boat.

00:01:47.702 --> 00:01:50.819
It has three bedrooms, two bathrooms.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:53.195
It has a washer/dryer.

00:01:53.195 --> 00:01:56.475
I've got a full-sized kitchen
with full-sized refrigerator

00:01:56.475 --> 00:01:58.852
and electric stove, pretty
much everything you could need.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.700
You go here and go down to the right.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:02.533
- [Niki] Oh?

00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:03.366
- [Garrett] Is there a downstairs?

00:02:03.366 --> 00:02:05.085
- [Lisa] Yeah, this is
the bedroom that people

00:02:05.085 --> 00:02:07.418
usually stay in, down there.

00:02:08.705 --> 00:02:09.596
- [Garrett] Oh wow.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.446
- [Niki] There?

00:02:10.446 --> 00:02:11.279
- [Garrett] Oh my goodness.

00:02:11.279 --> 00:02:12.308
- [Lisa] Yeah, so it's pretty comfy.

00:02:12.308 --> 00:02:15.792
- [Garrett] It actually
looks really cool and oh wow.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:17.573
Look at that, you're
like right at eye level

00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:18.449
with the water.

00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:19.810
- That's cool.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.905
- Yeah, this is like a little hideaway.

00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:22.988
- Wow, boats.

00:02:24.012 --> 00:02:25.777
- The challenges are probably storage.

00:02:25.777 --> 00:02:29.449
The biggest surprise is how
little I could make do with.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.963
I moved from a 5,000 square
foot house and put everything

00:02:32.963 --> 00:02:36.373
into a U-Haul with my two
cats and drove out here.

00:02:36.373 --> 00:02:39.956
This is where I love
to sit in the evening.

00:02:41.179 --> 00:02:43.512
The sun sets right over
there, it's beautiful.

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:44.483
- [Garrett] Oh my gosh, look at your view.

00:02:44.483 --> 00:02:45.903
- Well, dumb question.

00:02:45.903 --> 00:02:46.986
Does it rock?

00:02:49.061 --> 00:02:50.178
- This is ... no.

00:02:50.178 --> 00:02:53.517
I mean, this is so wide
and the bottom is flat.

00:02:53.517 --> 00:02:55.607
It doesn't rock much at all.

00:02:55.607 --> 00:02:58.198
- [Niki] This is awesome.

00:02:58.198 --> 00:02:59.630
- Lisa, we're not just saying
that because the cameras

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.521
are rolling, this is like--

00:03:00.521 --> 00:03:02.368
- [Lisa] I knew you
guys were gonna like it.

00:03:02.368 --> 00:03:04.459
- Niki and I are friends now.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.715
We're definitely work friends.

00:03:05.715 --> 00:03:08.037
In the meantime, Niki got
married, which I'm very happy

00:03:08.037 --> 00:03:08.890
for her.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.090
- He did not come to the wedding

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.025
even though he was all ...

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:16.164
- So nice to finally meet you
guys, come to your wedding.

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:18.696
- He did get us a gift
which was very nice.

00:03:18.696 --> 00:03:19.746
He didn't have to do that.

00:03:19.746 --> 00:03:20.663
Here we go.

00:03:22.165 --> 00:03:24.095
I'm very excited about this.

00:03:24.095 --> 00:03:25.496
- Home buddies, sweet home buddies.

00:03:25.496 --> 00:03:27.222
- So Garrett and I have lived
together on two occasions now,

00:03:27.222 --> 00:03:29.204
this will be our third
time living together.

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:31.889
- To keep building this
relationship, I think we need

00:03:31.889 --> 00:03:34.862
to figure out how to
move past work friends

00:03:34.862 --> 00:03:36.602
into like friends-friends.

00:03:36.602 --> 00:03:39.692
- [Niki] I'm gonna go
in here because I think

00:03:39.692 --> 00:03:41.218
this is the easiest.

00:03:41.218 --> 00:03:43.769
- Which means I go down below.

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:45.241
I hope there are no kitty cats.

00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:46.240
- Are you allergic to cats?

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.073
- Yeah.

00:03:47.073 --> 00:03:47.982
- Uh oh.

00:03:47.982 --> 00:03:50.464
- My goal for the houseboat
is to see if we can

00:03:50.464 --> 00:03:53.348
make plans to hang out outside of work

00:03:53.348 --> 00:03:55.011
because I think that will
be the actual difference

00:03:55.011 --> 00:03:56.716
between work friends and real friends.

00:03:56.716 --> 00:03:58.436
- This is so cozy.

00:03:58.436 --> 00:03:59.269
- Niki?

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:00.164
- [Niki] What?

00:04:00.164 --> 00:04:01.307
- You need any baskets?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.224
I have extras.

00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:03.980
- [Niki] You have baskets,
what kind of baskets?

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.071
- Extra baskets.

00:04:05.071 --> 00:04:05.950
Get off of my bed.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:06.934
- No.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.609
- [Garrett] I fit perfect, look.

00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:11.185
- I also fit perfect.

00:04:11.185 --> 00:04:12.018
- Look at you.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.291
You're actually adorable.

00:04:13.291 --> 00:04:14.977
- I'm an introvert, Garrett is not.

00:04:14.977 --> 00:04:17.543
My goal is to find some alone time.

00:04:17.543 --> 00:04:18.746
That's not to be antisocial.

00:04:18.746 --> 00:04:20.290
That's not because I don't like Garrett.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.571
For me to be a sane
and caring human being,

00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:25.287
I need some time alone.

00:04:25.287 --> 00:04:27.864
Look at all this space.

00:04:27.864 --> 00:04:29.039
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:04:29.039 --> 00:04:29.872
- To our houseboat.

00:04:29.872 --> 00:04:30.872
- Houseboat.

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:36.193
- You actually drank alcohol.

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:38.069
- I've tasted it before,
I'm not gonna drink that.

00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:40.214
- But doesn't it taste better on a boat?

00:04:40.214 --> 00:04:41.047
- Sure.

00:04:43.065 --> 00:04:46.126
- Today was day one on the houseboat.

00:04:46.126 --> 00:04:49.003
I expected the houseboat to
be so much smaller than it is.

00:04:49.003 --> 00:04:51.474
- It totally feels like we're
living in a normal apartment

00:04:51.474 --> 00:04:53.307
but we're on the water.

00:04:53.307 --> 00:04:56.830
- We're a lot closer to the
neighbors than I thought.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:57.663
- Hello.

00:04:59.746 --> 00:05:01.433
- Good.
- How are you?

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.455
- Sound travels so much freer.

00:05:04.455 --> 00:05:07.464
(dog barks)

00:05:07.464 --> 00:05:08.664
What is that?

00:05:08.664 --> 00:05:10.365
- Garrett and I have our
own rooms, which I think is

00:05:10.365 --> 00:05:11.551
really gonna help this experience.

00:05:11.551 --> 00:05:14.388
I have my own space and
I can close the door.

00:05:14.388 --> 00:05:16.198
- Lisa was telling us about
all these different kinds

00:05:16.198 --> 00:05:17.276
of activities.

00:05:17.276 --> 00:05:18.681
I think we're gonna go sailing tomorrow.

00:05:18.681 --> 00:05:20.191
That's gonna be unbelievable.

00:05:20.191 --> 00:05:23.730
- I feel like, for the first
time, Garrett and I don't

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.989
have to be thinking so hard
about where we're living

00:05:26.989 --> 00:05:29.923
and I think that will allow
for our relationship to grow

00:05:29.923 --> 00:05:32.513
in a way that it hasn't
been able to in the past.

00:05:32.513 --> 00:05:36.680
- My nose is getting congested
because of these cats.

00:05:39.808 --> 00:05:40.641
Good night, Niki.

00:05:40.641 --> 00:05:41.572
You look very cozy.

00:05:41.572 --> 00:05:42.558
- I am.

00:05:42.558 --> 00:05:44.393
- Okay, lights out, young lady.

00:05:44.393 --> 00:05:46.560
- [Niki] Okay, good night.

00:05:57.814 --> 00:05:59.782
- Good morning.

00:05:59.782 --> 00:06:02.492
It's actually a really beautiful morning.

00:06:02.492 --> 00:06:04.449
Oh, look, another one.

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:06.946
There are basically two
times when being 6'7" sucks.

00:06:06.946 --> 00:06:08.095
One is on airplanes.

00:06:08.095 --> 00:06:10.861
Two is anytime you have to shower.

00:06:10.861 --> 00:06:13.762
The boat actually has two
showers, but they're used

00:06:13.762 --> 00:06:17.929
for storage so we have to go
use the showers in the marina.

00:06:19.715 --> 00:06:21.965
I'm in the shower, kind of.

00:06:44.079 --> 00:06:46.246
Hey Niki, you want coffee?

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:01.002
Okay, it's brewing.

00:07:01.002 --> 00:07:02.825
- Thank you.

00:07:02.825 --> 00:07:06.509
- [Garrett] Good morning, happy Friday.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:09.194
- [Niki] What are you doing?

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:10.382
- Shaving, Niki.

00:07:10.382 --> 00:07:12.636
It's a natural part of a boy's body.

00:07:12.636 --> 00:07:14.866
By the way, the little
hairs go into the ocean.

00:07:14.866 --> 00:07:16.629
Same reason why I'm cutting
my fingernails here.

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:17.672
- [Niki] Are you serious?

00:07:17.672 --> 00:07:18.505
- Yeah.

00:07:18.505 --> 00:07:19.943
- That way you don't have to worry about--

00:07:19.943 --> 00:07:21.909
- Eww.
- Them flying everywhere.

00:07:21.909 --> 00:07:24.583
- This is really gross.

00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:26.228
- It's not that gross.

00:07:26.228 --> 00:07:27.961
A lot of people with dogs
walking by and looking at me

00:07:27.961 --> 00:07:30.910
like I'm kind of a weirdo.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.827
But that's boat living.

00:07:33.908 --> 00:07:36.150
- Lisa's neighbors usually
join her for breakfast

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.654
in her lobby area.

00:07:37.654 --> 00:07:40.702
So a few of them are joining
us for coffee this morning

00:07:40.702 --> 00:07:41.793
and then her friend her friend Chuck

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:43.053
is gonna take us out sailing.

00:07:43.053 --> 00:07:44.257
What are you doing, Garrett?

00:07:44.257 --> 00:07:46.806
- Making you eggs before we go sailing.

00:07:46.806 --> 00:07:48.806
- [Niki] Yay, thank you.

00:07:49.719 --> 00:07:51.136
- You're welcome.

00:07:59.181 --> 00:08:01.366
- I'll get us by this barge
and then I'm gonna turn

00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:03.171
this over to you, okay?

00:08:03.171 --> 00:08:07.338
Steering is on of the things
I can teach you the fastest.

00:08:12.415 --> 00:08:14.832
(soft music)

00:08:18.262 --> 00:08:20.554
- [Niki] Sailing was so
amazing and Chuck let us steer

00:08:20.554 --> 00:08:22.242
for a little while.

00:08:22.242 --> 00:08:25.995
- [Garrett] Blown away with
how good Niki was at sailing.

00:08:25.995 --> 00:08:29.099
She was doing these
complicated steering maneuvers

00:08:29.099 --> 00:08:33.005
while he was tacking the
sails back and forth.

00:08:33.005 --> 00:08:34.096
It was really amazing
to behold and we did it

00:08:34.096 --> 00:08:35.429
for three hours.

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.621
- After sailing, Garrett
and I went kayaking

00:08:45.621 --> 00:08:46.972
for a little while.

00:08:46.972 --> 00:08:47.805
Stroke!

00:08:49.413 --> 00:08:52.277
After that whole day on the
water, I was pretty ready

00:08:52.277 --> 00:08:54.099
to find some alone time.

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:55.653
- The thing about living in a
houseboat is that everything

00:08:55.653 --> 00:08:57.703
is wet, these shorts are wet.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:59.874
The shorts I'm wearing now are wet.

00:08:59.874 --> 00:09:01.952
This shirt is wet.

00:09:01.952 --> 00:09:03.168
This shirt is wet.

00:09:03.168 --> 00:09:07.949
- I found the perfect spot
here on this houseboat.

00:09:07.949 --> 00:09:12.116
I'm on the top deck hammock
chair with a great view.

00:09:13.121 --> 00:09:17.614
- Niki, I noticed went
upstairs to read alone.

00:09:17.614 --> 00:09:20.069
- Garrett came up to join me
and it was one of those things

00:09:20.069 --> 00:09:23.743
where like when your new
friends and there's nothing

00:09:23.743 --> 00:09:26.846
to talk about and silence
can be kind of awkward.

00:09:26.846 --> 00:09:28.978
It was totally fine and I
didn't feel awkward at all.

00:09:28.978 --> 00:09:31.461
I didn't feel like I
needed to fill that space.

00:09:31.461 --> 00:09:34.175
- Being near each other
but not really interacting,

00:09:34.175 --> 00:09:36.306
just sort of knowing the
other person was there.

00:09:36.306 --> 00:09:38.968
If either of us needed
anything, we were there

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:40.220
for each other.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.191
- I think that was a
really interesting step

00:09:42.191 --> 00:09:43.082
in our relationship.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.610
- Niki and I are about to go to dinner.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:47.193
We had a pretty incredible day.

00:09:48.467 --> 00:09:51.533
I think if I said, "Hey would
you want to hang outside

00:09:51.533 --> 00:09:52.463
of work?"

00:09:52.463 --> 00:09:53.758
She'd say yes.

00:09:53.758 --> 00:09:57.341
So at dinner tonight,
I think I'm gonna try

00:09:58.623 --> 00:10:00.206
to achieve my goal.

00:10:02.607 --> 00:10:06.182
So we just finished dinner
but the place was very loud

00:10:06.182 --> 00:10:09.463
so there was never really
a time for me to ask

00:10:09.463 --> 00:10:10.463
so I didn't.

00:10:12.513 --> 00:10:14.509
I thought I was going to.

00:10:14.509 --> 00:10:19.260
We're only in this houseboat
for another 12 hours

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.921
so hopefully, tomorrow
morning I will ask her.

00:10:22.921 --> 00:10:24.147
I don't know, we'll see.

00:10:24.147 --> 00:10:26.914
- This time has flown by
because we've had so much fun

00:10:26.914 --> 00:10:28.224
and I really enjoyed being here.

00:10:28.224 --> 00:10:30.815
It's kind of sad that
we're leaving tomorrow.

00:10:30.815 --> 00:10:33.109
This is the third time Niki
and I have lived together.

00:10:33.109 --> 00:10:37.118
What happens so far, every
time, is that sometime

00:10:37.118 --> 00:10:39.695
on the second night, she
and I start talking about

00:10:39.695 --> 00:10:41.112
really real shit.

00:10:42.317 --> 00:10:44.395
It's really wonderful.

00:10:44.395 --> 00:10:45.730
- It was like the first
time that Garrett and I

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:46.768
were really alone.

00:10:46.768 --> 00:10:48.860
He was telling me about this
job that he used to have.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.021
He asked about the wedding.

00:10:50.021 --> 00:10:52.761
It was like, for a moment
there, felt like old friends

00:10:52.761 --> 00:10:53.761
catching up.

00:10:58.052 --> 00:11:02.219
- Wow, of course, it is a
gorgeous freaking morning.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.693
(cat meows)

00:11:05.693 --> 00:11:09.436
This thing has been making
noise at me all morning.

00:11:09.436 --> 00:11:10.269
- [Niki] Good morning.

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:11.223
- Good morning.

00:11:11.223 --> 00:11:13.535
- [Niki] Good morning, Lolly.

00:11:13.535 --> 00:11:15.178
- I think, at some point in my life,

00:11:15.178 --> 00:11:16.802
I actually could live here.

00:11:16.802 --> 00:11:18.539
- Being on the water is
something that is actually

00:11:18.539 --> 00:11:20.077
really fun, I really enjoy it.

00:11:20.077 --> 00:11:21.752
- This part of the country is gorgeous.

00:11:21.752 --> 00:11:22.885
Look at this.

00:11:22.885 --> 00:11:24.208
Waking up to this every morning?

00:11:24.208 --> 00:11:25.301
That's unbelievable.

00:11:25.301 --> 00:11:29.881
Hey Nik, do you want to
get brunch next week?

00:11:29.881 --> 00:11:31.186
- Yeah.

00:11:31.186 --> 00:11:34.369
- [Garrett] Like on Saturday?

00:11:34.369 --> 00:11:35.452
- Yeah, okay.

00:11:36.935 --> 00:11:39.181
After living on this
houseboat with Garrett,

00:11:39.181 --> 00:11:40.350
it is definitely a place
that has brought us

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.183
closer together.

00:11:41.183 --> 00:11:42.832
We had enough time to be in our own spaces

00:11:42.832 --> 00:11:46.050
and our own rooms but also
we did so many fun activities

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.786
together, we went
sailing, we went kayaking.

00:11:48.786 --> 00:11:52.443
We had great space to just
sit and enjoy coffee together.

00:11:52.443 --> 00:11:53.806
- Now we're starting from like friends,

00:11:53.806 --> 00:11:55.778
becoming a better and better friend

00:11:55.778 --> 00:11:58.843
actually takes a lot of
intimate work and I'm excited

00:11:58.843 --> 00:11:59.676
to go to brunch.

00:11:59.676 --> 00:12:03.936
- Or maybe when we're both 80,
we'll be houseboat neighbors.

00:12:03.936 --> 00:12:05.829
- Bye houseboat.

00:12:05.829 --> 00:12:07.746
- [Niki] Bye houseboat.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:12.141
- It's brunch.

00:12:12.141 --> 00:12:15.314
We did it, we're getting
quick brunch but still counts.

00:12:15.314 --> 00:12:17.064
Happy Saturday, Niki.

00:12:19.362 --> 00:12:21.945
(upbeat music)

